{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNhoimkKFVe9oeNH4pDrph","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd083-truncate\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/truncate: Shrink or Extend File Size\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD truncate that differs from GNU truncate in flag syntax and relative\n6\t  size adjustment support. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gtruncate, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Set or adjust the size of files.\n12\t  - G2: Support absolute and relative size specifications with unit suffixes.\n13\t  - G3: Support reference file sizing.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtruncate via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Size specification\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"-s SIZE or --size=SIZE must set each FILE's size to SIZE bytes. SIZE may include unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000).\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"SIZE may be prefixed with + or - for relative adjustment (grow or shrink), < to set at most SIZE, > to set at least SIZE, / to round down to multiple, % to round up to multiple.\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the same size operation to each.\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"-c or --no-create must not create files that do not exist. Without -c, missing files are created.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Reference file\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-r RFILE or --reference=RFILE must use the size of RFILE as the base size instead of an explicit SIZE. Can be combined with -s for relative adjustment from the reference size.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: Must exit 1 if the reference file cannot be accessed.\n36\t\n37\t  R3:\n38\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R3.1:\n41\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n42\t      - R3.2:\n43\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, created, or resized, or when SIZE is invalid.\n44\t      - R3.3:\n45\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n46\t\n47\tnon_goals:\n48\t  - cmd/truncate does not implement sparse file optimization.\n49\t\n50\tpackage_contract:\n51\t  imports:\n52\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n53\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n54\t\n55\tacceptance_criteria:\n56\t  - id: AC1\n57\t    criterion: \"truncate -s 100 file creates or resizes file to 100 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n58\t    traces:\n59\t      - R1.1\n60\t      - R1.3\n61\t      - R1.4\n62\t  - id: AC2\n63\t    criterion: \"truncate -s +50 file grows file by 50 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.2\n66\t  - id: AC3\n67\t    criterion: \"truncate -r ref file sets file to ref's size, matching gtruncate.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R2.1\n70\t  - id: AC4\n71\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtruncate passes for all required test cases.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R2.1\n77\t  - id: AC5\n78\t    criterion: \"cmd/truncate compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.3\n83\t      - R1.4\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t      - R2.2\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"531186a7-5f3d-438b-ae9d-9dced46bcde5","uuid":"235582c2-301c-4938-96a5-fc877a21190d","timestamp":"2026-05-23T16:47:46.079Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5544/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml","content":"id: srd083-truncate\ntitle: \"cmd/truncate: Shrink or Extend File Size\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD truncate that differs from GNU truncate in flag syntax and relative\n  size adjustment support. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gtruncate, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Set or adjust the size of files.\n  - G2: Support absolute and relative size specifications with unit suffixes.\n  - G3: Support reference file sizing.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gtruncate via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Size specification\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"-s SIZE or --size=SIZE must set each FILE's size to SIZE bytes. SIZE may include unit suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers of 1000).\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"SIZE may be prefixed with + or - for relative adjustment (grow or shrink), < to set at most SIZE, > to set at least SIZE, / to round down to multiple, % to round up to multiple.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the same size operation to each.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-c or --no-create must not create files that do not exist. Without -c, missing files are created.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Reference file\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-r RFILE or --reference=RFILE must use the size of RFILE as the base size instead of an explicit SIZE. Can be combined with -s for relative adjustment from the reference size.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 if the reference file cannot be accessed.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, created, or resized, or when SIZE is invalid.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/truncate does not implement sparse file optimization.\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"truncate -s 100 file creates or resizes file to 100 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"truncate -s +50 file grows file by 50 bytes, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"truncate -r ref file sets file to ref's size, matching gtruncate.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtruncate passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/truncate compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PCTNMwaBkq3eo2u7CnZHV3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fq9F81ZbmTBm6QmXfdpKRx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5544/cmd/truncate/main.go"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198698,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":198698},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"531186a7-5f3d-438b-ae9d-9dced46bcde5","uuid":"9ae716e1-8586-4ffd-8c75-3a94ce7c35ff"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fq9F81ZbmTBm6QmXfdpKRx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage main\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"fmt\"\n8\t\t\"os\"\n9\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n10\t\t\"strings\"\n11\t\t\"syscall\"\n12\t\n13\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sizeparse\"\n14\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n15\t)\n16\t\n17\tconst helpText = `Usage: truncate OPTION... FILE...\n18\tShrink or extend the size of each FILE to the specified size\n19\t\n20\tA FILE argument that does not exist is created.\n21\t\n22\tIf a FILE is larger than the specified size, the extra data is lost.\n23\tIf a FILE is shorter, it is extended and the sparse extended part (hole)\n24\treads as zero bytes.\n25\t\n26\tMandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.\n27\t  -c, --no-create        do not create any files\n28\t  -o, --io-blocks        treat SIZE as number of IO blocks instead of bytes\n29\t  -r, --reference=RFILE  base size on RFILE\n30\t  -s, --size=SIZE        set or adjust the file size by SIZE bytes\n31\t      --help     display this help and exit\n32\t      --version  output version information and exit\n33\t\n34\tThe SIZE argument is an integer and optional unit (example: 10K is 10*1024).\n35\tUnits are K,M,G,T,P,E,Z,Y,R,Q (powers of 1024) or KB,MB,... (powers of 1000).\n36\tBinary prefixes can be used, too: KiB=K, MiB=M, and so on.\n37\t\n38\tSIZE may also be prefixed by one of the following modifying characters:\n39\t'+' extend by, '-' reduce by, '<' at most, '>' at least,\n40\t'/' round down to multiple of, '%' round up to multiple of.\n41\t`\n42\t\n43\tconst versionText = `truncate (go-unix-utils) dev\n44\t`\n45\t\n46\ttype options struct {\n47\t\tnoCreate  bool\n48\t\tioBlocks  bool\n49\t\treference string\n50\t\tsizeStr   string\n51\t\tsizeSet   bool\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\tfunc main() {\n55\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n56\t\topts, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n57\t\tif err != nil {\n58\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: %s\\n\", err)\n59\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'truncate --help' for more information.\\n\")\n60\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n61\t\t}\n62\t\tif !opts.sizeSet && opts.reference == \"\" {\n63\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: you must specify either '--size' or '--reference'\\n\")\n64\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'truncate --help' for more information.\\n\")\n65\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n66\t\t}\n67\t\tif len(files) == 0 {\n68\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: missing file operand\\n\")\n69\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'truncate --help' for more information.\\n\")\n70\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n71\t\t}\n72\t\tos.Exit(run(opts, files))\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\tfunc run(opts options, files []string) int {\n76\t\tvar baseSize int64\n77\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n78\t\t\tfi, err := os.Stat(opts.reference)\n79\t\t\tif err != nil {\n80\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: cannot stat %s: %s\\n\",\n81\t\t\t\t\tquote(opts.reference), errMsg(err))\n82\t\t\t\treturn 1\n83\t\t\t}\n84\t\t\tbaseSize = fi.Size()\n85\t\t}\n86\t\n87\t\tvar modifier byte\n88\t\tvar sizeVal int64\n89\t\tif opts.sizeSet {\n90\t\t\tvar err error\n91\t\t\tmodifier, sizeVal, err = parseSize(opts.sizeStr)\n92\t\t\tif err != nil {\n93\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: %s\\n\", err)\n94\t\t\t\treturn 1\n95\t\t\t}\n96\t\t\tif opts.ioBlocks {\n97\t\t\t\tsizeVal *= ioBlockSize(files[0])\n98\t\t\t}\n99\t\t}\n100\t\n101\t\texitCode := 0\n102\t\tfor _, path := range files {\n103\t\t\tif err := truncateFile(opts, path, baseSize, modifier, sizeVal); err != nil {\n104\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"truncate: %s\\n\", err)\n105\t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n106\t\t\t}\n107\t\t}\n108\t\treturn exitCode\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\tfunc truncateFile(opts options, path string, baseSize int64, modifier byte, sizeVal int64) error {\n112\t\tfi, err := ensureFile(opts, path)\n113\t\tif err != nil {\n114\t\t\treturn err\n115\t\t}\n116\t\tif fi == nil {\n117\t\t\treturn nil\n118\t\t}\n119\t\tnewSize, err := computeSize(opts, fi.Size(), baseSize, modifier, sizeVal)\n120\t\tif err != nil {\n121\t\t\treturn err\n122\t\t}\n123\t\tif err := os.Truncate(path, newSize); err != nil {\n124\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"cannot open %s for writing: %s\",\n125\t\t\t\tquote(path), errMsg(err))\n126\t\t}\n127\t\treturn nil\n128\t}\n129\t\n130\tfunc ensureFile(opts options, path string) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n131\t\tfi, err := os.Stat(path)\n132\t\tif err != nil && os.IsNotExist(err) {\n133\t\t\tif opts.noCreate {\n134\t\t\t\treturn nil, nil\n135\t\t\t}\n136\t\t\tf, createErr := os.Create(path)\n137\t\t\tif createErr != nil {\n138\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cannot open %s for writing: %s\",\n139\t\t\t\t\tquote(path), errMsg(createErr))\n140\t\t\t}\n141\t\t\tf.Close()\n142\t\t\tfi, err = os.Stat(path)\n143\t\t}\n144\t\tif err != nil {\n145\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cannot open %s for writing: %s\",\n146\t\t\t\tquote(path), errMsg(err))\n147\t\t}\n148\t\treturn fi, nil\n149\t}\n150\t\n151\tfunc computeSize(opts options, currentSize, baseSize int64, modifier byte, sizeVal int64) (int64, error) {\n152\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" && !opts.sizeSet {\n153\t\t\treturn baseSize, nil\n154\t\t}\n155\t\tbase := baseSize\n156\t\tif opts.reference == \"\" {\n157\t\t\tbase = currentSize\n158\t\t}\n159\t\tresult, err := applySize(base, modifier, sizeVal)\n160\t\tif err != nil {\n161\t\t\treturn 0, err\n162\t\t}\n163\t\tif result < 0 {\n164\t\t\treturn 0, nil\n165\t\t}\n166\t\treturn result, nil\n167\t}\n168\t\n169\tfunc applySize(current int64, modifier byte, size int64) (int64, error) {\n170\t\tswitch modifier {\n171\t\tcase 0:\n172\t\t\treturn size, nil\n173\t\tcase '+':\n174\t\t\treturn current + size, nil\n175\t\tcase '-':\n176\t\t\treturn current - size, nil\n177\t\tcase '<':\n178\t\t\tif current < size {\n179\t\t\t\treturn current, nil\n180\t\t\t}\n181\t\t\treturn size, nil\n182\t\tcase '>':\n183\t\t\tif current > size {\n184\t\t\t\treturn current, nil\n185\t\t\t}\n186\t\t\treturn size, nil\n187\t\tcase '/':\n188\t\t\tif size == 0 {\n189\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"division by zero\")\n190\t\t\t}\n191\t\t\treturn (current / size) * size, nil\n192\t\tcase '%':\n193\t\t\tif size == 0 {\n194\t\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"division by zero\")\n195\t\t\t}\n196\t\t\treturn ((current + size - 1) / size) * size, nil\n197\t\t}\n198\t\treturn size, nil\n199\t}\n200\t\n201\tfunc parseSize(s string) (byte, int64, error) {\n202\t\tif s == \"\" {\n203\t\t\treturn 0, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"Invalid number: %s\", quote(s))\n204\t\t}\n205\t\tvar modifier byte\n206\t\trest := s\n207\t\tif len(rest) > 0 {\n208\t\t\tswitch rest[0] {\n209\t\t\tcase '+', '-', '<', '>', '/', '%':\n210\t\t\t\tmodifier = rest[0]\n211\t\t\t\trest = rest[1:]\n212\t\t\t}\n213\t\t}\n214\t\tif rest == \"\" {\n215\t\t\treturn 0, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"Invalid number: %s\", quote(s))\n216\t\t}\n217\t\tval, err := sizeparse.Parse(rest)\n218\t\tif err != nil {\n219\t\t\treturn 0, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"Invalid number: %s\", quote(s))\n220\t\t}\n221\t\treturn modifier, val, nil\n222\t}\n223\t\n224\tfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string, error) {\n225\t\tvar opts options\n226\t\tvar files []string\n227\t\tendFlags := false\n228\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n229\t\t\targ := args[i]\n230\t\t\tif endFlags || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n231\t\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n232\t\t\t\tcontinue\n233\t\t\t}\n234\t\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n235\t\t\t\tendFlags = true\n236\t\t\t\tcontinue\n237\t\t\t}\n238\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n239\t\t\t\tadv, err := parseLongFlag(arg, args[i+1:], &opts)\n240\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n241\t\t\t\t\treturn options{}, nil, err\n242\t\t\t\t}\n243\t\t\t\ti += adv\n244\t\t\t\tcontinue\n245\t\t\t}\n246\t\t\tadv, err := parseShortFlags(arg[1:], args[i+1:], &opts)\n247\t\t\tif err != nil {\n248\t\t\t\treturn options{}, nil, err\n249\t\t\t